| Flow Rate | RunData/System flow |
| UV Absorbance | RunData/UV 1, UV 2 or UV 3 |
| Pressure | RunData/System pressure |
| Gradient | RunData/Conc B |

The listed addresses are candidates and require verification.

For each parameter, capture:

- Exact NodeId.
- Complete browse path.
- Current value.
- OPC data type.
- Engineering units.
- Exact quality code.
- Timestamp.
- Current instrument operating state.
- Parameter semantics.
- Existing UDT member path.

Monitor the values for at least 60–120 seconds.

Do not classify Good_NoData as valid live data.

Do not treat sentinel values as actual process measurements.

Determine whether valid scalar measurements become available following View-mode initialization while the instrument is idle.

If valid measurements require an active method or manual run, document the limitation and prepare a follow-on observation during a TBMC-operated run.

Do not initiate equipment operation to generate data.

